ll ROWAN","mensTime":"08:59:00"}},"narrative":"The 1977 Comrades Marathon was the 52nd running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 89.700 km. The race was held on Tuesday, 31 May. Conditions: Warm, sunny day. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nAlan ROBB claimed the men's title in 05:47:00, ahead of Steve ATKINS (05:57:00) and Dave WRIGHT (05:58:00). Lettie VAN ZYL won the women's race in 08:58:00, followed by Thea CLAASSEN (09:18:00).\n\nAlan ROBB's 05:47:00 set a new up record, beating Mick ORTON's 05:48:57 from 1972. Lettie VAN ZYL's 08:58:00 broke her own women's course record of 09:05:00 from 1976. Lettie VAN ZYL's 08:58:00 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1921 (Bill ROWAN, 08:59:00).\n\nFrom a field of 1,669 entries, 1,668 runners crossed the finish line (99.9% completion rate), with athletes representing over 8 countries. The field comprised 1,662 men and 6 women (0.4% female). The average finish time was 09:11:29.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 188 Silver, 1,470 Bronze. 618 runners (37.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was COWLING in 10:59:00.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1975, the field was 34.9% larger.","countryDataPct":100.0}